 "why": "LM_SW gets a via in U201 pin 3's pad and one in R204 pad 1; LM_UVLO's R204 to R205 link runs on F.Cu between vias in the two pads. VBAT_IN leaves pin 2 west on B.Cu, runs north between R204's pads and ends at a via at (147.9, 71.6) into a 0.6 mm VBAT_IN pour finger on In2 (zone PWR_VBAT_IN_U201_In2), which reaches the west VBAT_IN pour under the six lanes. The finger lies in In2's power-only region (y 70.2 to 70.8): a power shape, not a track, so the signal lines above it stay where they are.",
